have had  to come here to stay with family oh i  heard our home  and my brothers as a  burnt  gone  how does that make you feel knowing that  what do you think  everything's gone our whole livelihood  it's horrifying i'm just glad they all  made it out  it was a close it was a close call  yeah they said when they're just leaving  their home the flames were  in the back  behind the house  linton first nation has issued an  evacuation order for some of its  reserves it says the number of  structures lost to the fire has jumped  from three this morning to now sitting  in the double digits the regional  district here says an additional two  dozen homes have also been evacuated so  far the fire has stayed away from litten  itself which is east across the river  from this fire instead it's moving north  driven by strong winds today we're  expecting another low to move in and  bring winds 40 to 50 kilometers an hour  gusting 60. so the wind will continue to  be a challenge today as well the terrain  is really steep and poses a dangerous  activity to firefighters evacuees have  been sent north to the town of lilluet  to an evacuation shelter and some are  staying in the surrounding hotels but  space is running out fast leaving people  wondering where they'll go next nitu  kamil kermali reporting near linton bc  thanks kamil next a thorny visit how the  u.s president's historic trip to saudi  arabia sparked backlash  with his domestic agenda on the rocks  u.s president joe biden made a historic  journey today aboard air force one  flying direct from israel to saudi  arabia but that symbolic gesture  overshadowed by criticism over biden's  willingness to overlook saudi arabia's  human rights record and how desperately  biden needs cooperation from around the  region on a number of key issues jackson  proskow reports  for president joe biden each step of  this trip involves walking a political  and diplomatic tightrope from a fist  bump with the man accused of approving  the murder of jamal khashoggi to close  door meetings over a long list of mutual  concerns but the basic most elemental  thing is to send a message that america  is not pivoting to other parts of the  world that we're still sticking around  it's not that easy as a presidential  candidate biden declared saudi arabia a  pariah state and was reluctant to engage  with crown prince mohammed bin salman at  all  as president he now needs the saudis to  increase oil production as he faces a  political crisis at home over gas prices  and inflation biden insists he did not  waiver and raised khashoggi's murder  with the saudis before any other  business he basically said that he  he was not personally responsible for it  i indicated i thought he was  the four-day trip signals a larger shift  in middle east dynamics biden became the  first american president to fly directly  to saudi arabia from israel at a time  when he's hoping to unite two former  adversaries to confront a common threat  in iran biden's trip to the region also  included a visit to the west bank where  he met palestinian leaders and  reaffirmed support for a two-state  solution eventually even if the ground  is not ripe at this moment  to restart negotiations  the united states and my administration  will not give up on trying to bring the  palestinians israelis  and both sides closer together it's in  saudi arabia where biden is looking for  the biggest gains and facing the most  peril a delicate visit with a tenuous  ally  jackson prosko global news washington  firefighters and rescue teams searching  the wreckage of a number of buildings in  the ukrainian city of mikolav after  another round of russian missile strikes  [Applause]  ukrainian defense officials say 10  buildings were hit at least four people  were hurt in the early morning attacks  but firefighters managed to rescue a  puppy from the badly damaged building  the ukrainian government says their  recapture of snake island is allowing  for cargo ships carrying grain to enter  the black sea video posted by the  ukraine state border service shows cargo  ships being escorted by coast guard  vessels down the danube river to be  loaded with grain ukraine says 16 ships  have already started their journeys  while more than 90 others are waiting  their turn  coming up a man survives 18 hours lost  at sea thanks to an assist from an  unlikely flotation device  a tourist in greece is sharing an  amazing story of survival after he was  swept out to sea  the man identified only as ivan from  macedonia was swimming in the sea with  two friends when they were caught in a  powerful current and dragged far  offshore the greek coast guard was  notified and after a search the men were  declared lost at sea but ivan got lucky  as he was drifting he spotted a soccer  ball bobbing in the waves and grabbed it  he clung to the ball for 18 hours before  being spotted by a greek air force  helicopter and a rescue operation was  launched it turns out the owners of the  ball recognized it in greek news  coverage of the rescue it belongs to two  little boys who lost it in the waves 10  days before while playing on a beach  some 130 kilometers from where ivan was  found  one of the other men who was washed away  was also found safe while the third is  still missing  and that is global national for this  friday i'm nitu garcia tonight's your  canada is this pod of pelicans in the  heritage hills wetlands in sherwood park  alberta thanks for watching hope to see  you here again tomorrow  [Music]  you
 

